      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_4e1bb2150de3c7852463210e25712d6e5046722712ec1d15876ab3c38855cd1c",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The finite damped Möbius combinations are engineered so that a floor-function rewrite exposes their pointwise target before the topology is addressed. Passing n to infinity produces an explicit reciprocal-zeta correction, and then Möbius inversion identifies the ε-to-zero limit as −χ; none of this yet proves convergence in the Hilbert norm.",
